.TH HOBBYCAD 1 "2026-08-31" "hobbycad 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hobbycad \- parametric 3D CAD application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hobbycad
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B hobbycad
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B HobbyCAD
is a parametric 3D solid modeler built on the OpenCASCADE Technology (OCCT)
kernel with a Qt 6 interface. It provides boundary representation (B\-Rep)
modeling, sketching with a geometric constraint solver, and import and export
of common CAD interchange formats.
.PP
Given a
.IR file ,
HobbyCAD opens it. A directory is treated as a native project; see
.BR "FILE FORMATS" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information, including the OpenCASCADE version in use, and exit.
This is the quickest way to confirm which OCCT a build is running against.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gui
Start in interactive command\-line mode instead of the graphical interface.
Requires no display server.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " file.qss"
Load a custom Qt stylesheet. Overridden by
.BR HOBBYCAD_THEME .
.TP
.BI \-\-exec " command"
Execute one command as the graphical interface starts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI convert " input output"
Convert between file formats. The output format is taken from the output
file's extension unless
.BI \-\-format " fmt"
is given.
.TP
.BI script " file"
Execute a script file. A
.B \-
in place of
.I file
reads the script from standard input, so scripts may be piped. Pass
.B \-\-dry\-run
to validate a script without executing it.
.PP
Run
.B hobbycad
.I command
.B \-\-help
for options specific to a command.
.SH STARTUP MODES
HobbyCAD selects a mode at startup according to what the system supports.
.TP
.B Full Mode
The 3D viewport, used whenever OCCT can initialize one. This is the default.
.TP
.B Reduced Mode
A 2D canvas only, used when OpenGL is unavailable or when forced with
.BR HOBBYCAD_REDUCED_MODE .
File conversion and geometry operations remain available.
.TP
.B CLI Mode
An interactive terminal, entered with
.B \-\-no\-gui
or automatically when no display server is present. Type
.B help
at its prompt for the command list, which includes
.BR new ", " open ", " save ", " export ", " import ", " extrude
and
.BR sketch .
.SH FILE FORMATS
.TP
.B .hcad
Native HobbyCAD project. A directory containing a manifest rather than a
single file, so a project is opened by passing its directory.
.TP
.BR .brep ", " .brp
OpenCASCADE B\-Rep geometry.
.TP
.BR .step ", " .stp ", " .iges ", " .igs
Interchange formats for exchange with other CAD systems.
.TP
.BR .stl ", " .obj
Mesh formats, for 3D printing and rendering.
.TP
.BR .dxf ", " .svg
Two\-dimensional formats, used for sketch import and export.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOBBYCAD_THEME
Path to a Qt stylesheet
.RB ( .qss )
file. Consulted only when
.B \-\-theme
was not given, or named a stylesheet that could not be loaded. The full
order is
.BR \-\-theme ,
then this variable, then
.IR ~/.config/HobbyCAD/theme.qss ,
then the built\-in default.
.TP
.B HOBBYCAD_REDUCED_MODE
Set to
.B 1
to force Reduced Mode even where a 3D viewport would be possible. Useful
for testing, and on systems whose OpenGL support is present but unreliable.
.TP
.BR DISPLAY ", " WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Not read for configuration, but their presence decides the startup mode:
with neither set, HobbyCAD starts in CLI Mode as though
.B \-\-no\-gui
had been given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: a file could not be read or written, a conversion failed,
or a script reported an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the graphical interface, choosing a mode automatically:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad
.RE
.PP
Open a project directory, or a single geometry file:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad myproject/
.br
.B hobbycad model.brep
.RE
.PP
Work without a display server:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad \-\-no\-gui
.RE
.PP
Convert between formats without starting the interface:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad convert in.brep out.step
.RE
.PP
Run a script, or pipe one in:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad script myscript.txt
.br
.B cat myscript.txt | hobbycad script \-
.RE
.PP
Validate a script without running it:
.PP
.RS
.B hobbycad script \-\-dry\-run myscript.txt
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hobbycad/cli_history
Command\-line history kept between CLI sessions. Note the lower\-case
directory name, which differs from the one below.
.TP
.I ~/.config/HobbyCAD/theme.qss
Stylesheet loaded when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B HOBBYCAD_THEME
supplied one.
.TP
.I ~/.config/HobbyCAD/crash.log
Written if HobbyCAD terminates abnormally.
.TP
.I ~/.config/HobbyCAD/recovery/
Recovery data for documents open at the time of an abnormal exit.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/ayourk/hobbycad/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
The user manual installed with the package, and the project page at
.UR https://github.com/ayourk/hobbycad
.UE .
